Use case: stylized-concept. Create one polished, original Japanese anime-style 2D full-body character illustration, intended as the source image for building a humanoid 3D game character for a CoderDojo demonstration. One character centered in a tall portrait image, single straight-on front view at eye level. Entire figure from top of hair to soles of both shoes, with generous margins. Clean, crisp outlines, solid colors, restrained cel shading, even soft lighting, plain pale blue-gray background without floor shadow or props. No typography, watermark, panels or inset views.

Character: a 14-year-old girl, 140 cm tall, short and naturally slender with age-appropriate proportions. Energetic and cheerful with big dark eyes, a relatively wide mouth, and a bright natural open smile. Straight black short bob ending around the jaw, with clearly readable hair silhouette. Casual school uniform styling: opaque white button-front collared school shirt with sleeves rolled neatly to just below the elbows, blazer removed, gray pleated school skirt with hem a few centimeters above the knees, pink knit cardigan tied around the waist with its knot and sleeves legible, white loose socks, dark brown synthetic-leather school loafers. The shirt and skirt are fully opaque and the design has an everyday, wholesome school-portrait tone. A light-blue lace scrunchie on her LEFT wrist (viewer right). She is holding one compact iPhone SE with a solid pink case in her RIGHT hand (viewer left), with the case and single rear camera visible, fingers holding its edge. No other accessories.

Pose: both feet on the same plane with a little space between them. Natural nearly symmetric stance, both upper arms slightly angled outward so there is a visible gap between each arm and her torso. Keep the pink phone outside the silhouette of the torso and skirt and the left scrunchie visible. Clear separations between hair, torso, arms, garment layers, legs and footwear. No foreshortening, extreme perspective, stylized elongated limbs or cropped body parts.
